WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.479 --> 00:00:09.903
Long ago, in a faraway village in Africa, there lived a famous blacksmith.

2
00:00:10.544 --> 00:00:11.945
His name was Kintae.

3
00:00:12.606 --> 00:00:18.150
Every morning, people would come to watch him work, and he liked having the people nearby.

4
00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:23.855
He would hammer the red-hot iron, and the people would sing to his steady beat.

5
00:00:25.436 --> 00:00:31.724
One morning a messenger from the king's court ran to Kintae's home and said, "The king wants to

6
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:32.685
see you immediately.

7
00:00:33.185 --> 00:00:34.485
He has a job for you to do."

8
00:00:35.025 --> 00:00:36.566
Kintae was very happy.

9
00:00:37.186 --> 00:00:40.167
He quickly got dressed and hurried to the palace.

10
00:00:40.847 --> 00:00:43.928
He passed many of his friends as he walked to the palace.

11
00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:48.729
To each of them he said proudly: "The king has sent for me!

12
00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:50.370
He has a job for me!"

13
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.751
When Kintae reached the palace, he had to wait.

14
00:00:54.371 --> 00:00:57.772
While he waited, he wondered why the king had sent for him.

15
00:00:58.432 --> 00:01:05.037
Kintae often made things for the palace, but usually one of the king's servants told Kintae what to

16
00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:10.020
make. When Kintae saw the king, he bowed very low.

17
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.464
"You may stand," said the king, and Kintae stood.

18
00:01:14.484 --> 00:01:20.748
"I have sent for you," continued the king, "because I have a special task for you."

19
00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:25.972
The king clapped his hands, and servants carried in baskets full of iron.

20
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.901
They placed the baskets in front of Kintae.

21
00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:34.562
"You are to take this metal and make it into a man," said the king.

22
00:01:34.582 --> 00:01:40.904
"A real, living man who can walk, talk, think, and has blood in his veins."

23
00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:45.865
Kintae lowered his eyes because what the king asked was impossible.

24
00:01:46.546 --> 00:01:52.067
Kintae was also afraid because to say no to the king was the same as asking for death.

25
00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:59.335
Kintae did not want to die, so he again bowed very low and said, "Yes, Your Majesty."

26
00:02:00.175 --> 00:02:06.299
The king's servants carried the iron back to Kintae's shop, but as he followed, he kept his eyes

27
00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:09.381
lowered. Kintae knew his days were numbered.

28
00:02:09.982 --> 00:02:14.105
He spent his days and nights looking for a solution to his problem.

29
00:02:15.606 --> 00:02:17.607
His friends made many suggestions.

30
00:02:17.627 --> 00:02:21.670
"Couldn't you make an iron shell, so a man could get inside it?"

31
00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.311
suggested one friend.

32
00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:29.562
Another friend said, "I think you should run away to a faraway country and start life all over

33
00:02:29.602 --> 00:02:31.163
again where no one knows you."

34
00:02:32.004 --> 00:02:34.905
His friends meant well, but they couldn't help Kintae.

35
00:02:35.525 --> 00:02:37.647
He was so worried he became sick.

36
00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:44.630
He couldn't eat, he couldn't sleep, and he couldn't work because he couldn't think about anything except the

37
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:45.591
king's task.

38
00:02:46.471 --> 00:02:51.814
One evening, as he walked through a lonely area of the fields, he heard something strange.

39
00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:54.736
He went closer to find out what it was.

40
00:02:55.684 --> 00:03:00.045
As he got closer, he saw his boyhood friend singing to himself.

41
00:03:01.386 --> 00:03:04.887
Sadly, his old friend had gone mad a long time ago.

42
00:03:05.527 --> 00:03:08.067
He lived alone in the bush far from town.

43
00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.788
"Hi, Kintae," said his crazy boyhood friend.

44
00:03:11.808 --> 00:03:13.669
"Thank you for visiting me.

45
00:03:14.309 --> 00:03:16.830
I knew you were coming so I prepared this feast for us.

46
00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.090
Come, sit down."

47
00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:22.231
The meal wasn't really a feast, but it was delicious.

48
00:03:22.851 --> 00:03:24.652
They ate berries and some honey.

49
00:03:25.932 --> 00:03:28.873
Suddenly Kintae realized how hungry he was.

50
00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:33.034
This was the first food he had eaten in several days.

51
00:03:33.794 --> 00:03:39.096
The food made him feel better, and he began to tell his old friend about the king's task.

52
00:03:39.116 --> 00:03:43.257
"Well," finished Kintae, "that is my story."

53
00:03:43.277 --> 00:03:47.359
"I know what you must do," said his old friend immediately.

54
00:03:47.379 --> 00:03:51.240
"Go and tell the king that you need special ingredients for this task.

55
00:03:53.216 --> 00:03:58.500
Tell him you need one thousand carts of charcoal made from human hair, and one hundred buckets full

56
00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.380
of human tears."

57
00:04:00.141 --> 00:04:03.623
After his old friend said this, he laughed like a madman.

58
00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:08.727
Kintae thanked his friend for such good advice and then returned to the city.

59
00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:12.169
At first light, he hurried to the king's palace.

60
00:04:12.869 --> 00:04:15.351
When Kintae saw the king, he bowed low.

61
00:04:15.371 --> 00:04:19.014
"You may stand," said the king.

62
00:04:19.034 --> 00:04:20.735
"Why have you come?

63
00:04:21.275 --> 00:04:22.356
Is the man finished?"

64
00:04:22.896 --> 00:04:23.577
asked the king.

65
00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.439
Kintae said, "No, Your Majesty.

66
00:04:27.059 --> 00:04:29.461
I need special ingredients to complete your task."

67
00:04:30.042 --> 00:04:35.345
Kintae told the king what he needed, and the king ordered all his subjects to cut their hair

68
00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:37.207
and to cry into buckets.

69
00:04:37.907 --> 00:04:39.348
The people did their best.

70
00:04:40.249 --> 00:04:44.392
They shaved their heads and cried into their buckets, but it wasn't enough.

71
00:04:45.093 --> 00:04:49.236
Only two pots of tears and one load of charcoal were collected.

72
00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:53.169
When the king learned of these results, he sent for Kintae.

73
00:04:53.769 --> 00:04:56.750
Kintae was very afraid when he went back to the king.

74
00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:03.272
"Kintae," said the king, "you have asked me for something that is impossible.

75
00:05:03.892 --> 00:05:09.614
My people can never grow enough hair, nor cry enough tears to give you the ingredients you need.

76
00:05:10.414 --> 00:05:12.495
I therefore free you from your task."

77
00:05:13.215 --> 00:05:16.408
"Yes, Your Majesty," replied Kintae.

78
00:05:16.428 --> 00:05:18.991
As he walked away from the king, he took a breath.

79
00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:23.855
It felt like he hadn't breathed for weeks.

80
00:05:24.515 --> 00:05:28.018
He was happy again, and he smiled all the way home.

81
00:05:28.859 --> 00:05:33.864
As time went on, the king and his people forgot about Kintae's impossible task.

82
00:05:34.624 --> 00:05:37.407
But Kintae never forgot who had saved him.

83
00:05:38.127 --> 00:05:43.052
Kintae made sure that his old friend never felt hungry or thirsty again.
